      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good way to frame it. so if i'm teaching this, i'm assuming i should focus on the idea that the system itself is basically designed to preserve this inequality? like, is there really any merit to the argument that things like individual financial choices or different economic behaviors are significant drivers of the gap, or is that just a way to deflect from the structural issues you mentioned?",
